+# The logger is told to break the contract it emits into
+
+Status: needs-triage
+
+Found by 05's first pass, which cannot close until this lands. 05 keeps the pass
+that closes it; this ticket holds what the pass turned up and what 05's *whatever
+that pass says about the prompt* line was pointing at.
+
+**Read first**: `evals/logger/charter.md` (the seam's own lines), `docs/logging/eval-set.md`
+(what the thirty rows expect), CONTEXT.md § *What a report says*, ADR-0004.
+
+## The pass
+
+| figure | value |
+|---|---|
+| held | 24 of 90 runs — 30 rows x 3 repetitions, `gpt-oss:20b`, bar 100% |
+| the determined half | 7 of 50 valid runs |
+| the same 50, rescored on `log.to_performed` of what was emitted | 30 |
+| the must-ask half | 17 of 36 — derived from the two figures above, not measured apart |
+
+Most of what failed is the contract the document is emitted into, not the reading
+of the sentence. Two of the four findings are fixable without touching anything
+the charter reserves; two are not, and are named at the bottom rather than built.
+
+## 1. The prompt contradicts the schema, the validator and the set
+
+`coach/logger.py:126` says `assumed` is never the model's. `coach/logger.py:135`
+says an `assumed` number has to be the prescribed one and names the two places it
+stands. `coach/logger.py:130` says a value nobody gave is left out rather than
+filled in. Against that:
+
+| what actually holds | where |
+|---|---|
+| every property of a block is required; only `load_kg`, `load_kg_source` and `rpe` can be null | `tools.strict_schema` (`tools.py:587`), which the charter requires |
+| `assumed` stands where it equals the prescription, and where the prescription is silent | `log.py:499`, charter § Constrained |
+| expects `assumed` on exactly those values — U2, U3, U5, U9, U10, U11, U12, U13-U18 | `docs/logging/eval-set.md` |
+
+So a block that deviates in one value has to carry the other five, and the only
+honest label for the ones the user never gave is the one the prompt forbids. A
+model that believes the prompt has two moves left: label them `reported`, which is
+the document claiming the user said it, or write no block at all. Both are what the
+pass scored. It is also the likeliest reason the must-ask half leaks: with no
+*leave it out* available inside a block, asking is the only honest route to a value
+the report does not determine, and the prompt points at a third one that does not
+exist.
+
+**What stays the model's**: which blocks to write at all (charter § Free, *which
+values deviated and which are left out*). The leaving-out is real at block
+granularity and the prompt should say it there.
+
+### To build
+
+- `LOGGING` says what the emit schema requires: inside a block it writes, every
+  value is there, and a value the report does not determine is `ask_user`'s —
+  a criterion, not an answer.
+- The `assumed` rule stated once, in the validator's own terms: the prescription's
+  own number where there is a prescription, refused where the prescription says
+  otherwise or there is none behind the workout at all, and never on a load.
+- The bullet at `coach/logger.py:130` goes: it describes a shape the model is not
+  emitting into.
+- CONTEXT.md § *What a report says* names who may write `assumed`. Today it reads
+  *filled in by adherence*, which is where the prompt's version came from.
+- Tests: the prompt's claim about what a block must carry is **derived from
+  `tools.strict_schema(logs.PerformedWorkout)`**, never a copy of the sentence; and
+  nothing in `LOGGING` forbids a provenance `log.validate` accepts.
+
+## 2. The exclusion vocabulary is nowhere in the context
+
+The model has to emit a `value` that `exclusions.classify` resolves, and nothing it
+can see says what those words are: `LOGGING` gives two examples
+(`coach/logger.py:164`), `logger.brief` carries the date and the open workout, and
+`logger.KEEPS` trims every tool answer to id, name, equipment, mechanic and primary
+muscles — neither `movement_pattern` nor `loaded_joints` among them. A value that
+names neither is refused by `log.py:588`, and the refusal ends the run (finding 3).
+U13-U16 need `shoulder`, `vertical push`, `knee` and `lumbar spine` character for
+character.
+
+### To build
+
+- `brief` carries the catalog's movement patterns and its loaded joints, **read
+  from the data** at run time — `catalog.values(connection, "movement_pattern")`
+  and `catalog.joint_values`, never a list in Python.
+- One reader in `engine/exclusions.py`, which `classify` is rewritten onto, so the
+  words offered and the words accepted cannot drift.
+- Tests: every value offered to the model is one `classify` accepts, over the
+  fixture catalog; and no pattern or joint is spelled out in Python.
+
+This informs the judgement and does not take it: whether anything is implicated,
+and which word it is, stays the model's (charter § Free). `KEEPS` is not widened —
+it is a charter line, and these rows name a body part in the sentence rather than
+read one off an exercise.
+
+## What this ticket does not do
+
+Three decisions, none of them mine. The work above does not depend on any of them.
+
+**A repair turn.** Charter § Constrained: *exactly one emit call ... and no repair
+turn: a document that does not parse or does not validate ends the run as
+`refused`, and the model is never shown the refusal to try again.* The planner's
+`validate` sends named violations back and allows `ATTEMPTS = 3`
+(`coach/planner.py:38`, `:506`); the logger's ends the run. Moving it would buy the
+4 determined runs that produced nothing to score, and would turn every refused
+document into one more attempt instead of a `VALIDATOR` failure on top of its
+differences. It costs one more emit call per refused run — minutes each on this
+machine — and it is the line that currently makes a refused run a thing you read
+rather than a thing the model argues with.
+
+**The emitted form requiring every value.** Same line: *a strict JSON schema (every
+property required, no extras)*. Relaxing it would let the document say *the user
+never gave this* by omission, which is the shape the prompt was written against and
+the shape row U7's *skipped* needs. The prompt fix above is the version that leaves
+the line where it is.
+
+**What the suite scores.** Rescoring on the document the engine would write is what
+turned 7 into 30, and it is a change to the measurement's own standard:
+`docs/logging/eval-set.md` says only the deviations are written and that everything
+but two fields is equality. The set was written blind, and a standard that moves
+after the first pass measures the author rather than the agent.
+**Recommendation**: do not touch the scorer in this ticket. Fix the prompt, re-run,
+and decide with the second number in hand — if the model emits the deviation-only
+form the set expects, the equality scoring holds and nothing has to move.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- [ ] `LOGGING` and `log.validate` agree about `assumed`, asserted by a test that
+      reads the required properties off `tools.strict_schema(logs.PerformedWorkout)`.
+- [ ] The exclusion vocabulary reaches the model from the catalog, through the one
+      reader `classify` uses, asserted over the fixture.
+- [ ] `trainer eval --suite log` re-run on `gpt-oss:20b`, 3 repetitions, with
+      `TRAINER_DB` pointing at what `log_evaluation.prepared` built, and the number
+      written down here beside 24 of 90, per row rather than as one figure.
+- [ ] Both halves reported: the determined rows and the must-ask rows, so it is
+      visible which half moved.
+- [ ] The full test suite and mypy are green.
+- [ ] `/code-review` run, every finding fixed with a test or declined in writing.
+
+## Comments
+
+- **Numbering.** This is a sixth issue under a session whose slicing rule allows
+  five. The alternative is to carry it as 05's second half and close both under
+  05's roadmap line. Either way it is one roadmap edit, and it is the user's.
+- **Cost.** The re-run is local and free, and it is hours of wall clock. Nothing
+  here needs Groq; if the user wants the same pass on Groq to separate the model
+  from the contract, that is a paid run and needs a budget agreed first.
+- **U7 stays as it is.** The shape still cannot say *not performed*, the set says so
+  itself, and the row goes on measuring only that nothing was invented.
